  "body": "CamCraft ships the Makera Z1 (`assets/machines/makera-z1.mch`, #868). It does not ship the Makera Z1 Pro.\n\nThe Z1 Pro has the same frame as the Z1:\n- Envelope: 200 x 200 x 100 mm.\n- Spindle: 150 W, 0-13000 rpm.\n- Coolant: air blast (M7).\n\nThe Pro has closed-loop steppers and ball screws. Its maximum travel speed is 2000 mm/min. The Z1 maximum is 1200 mm/min.\n\nSource: Makera's public Z1 page (https://global.makera.com/pages/makera-z1, \"Max: Z1 1200mm/min; Z1 Pro 2000mm/min\").\n\nThe G-code dialect is the same for the Makera machines. The machine file holds the limits. Thus the Z1 Pro needs a machine file only. It names the shared \"Makera Carvera\" post.\n\nDone means:\n- `assets/machines/makera-z1-pro.mch` is a built-in machine with X/Y/Z feed and rapid ceilings of 2000 mm/min.\n- The machine names the \"Makera Carvera\" post.\n- `crates/app/tests/makera_z1.rs` pins the figures, the M7/M9 output and the travel and spindle refusals for the Z1 and the Z1 Pro.\n\nSuggested labels (the reporter cannot set labels): `enhancement`, `area:post`, `P6`, `effort:low`.\n",
